.TH OCELOTLC 1 "August 2026" "Ocelotl Tensor Compiler 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ocelotlc \- experimental LLVM-based native compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocelotlc
.I source-file
.B --emit-tokens

.B ocelotlc
.I source-file
.B --emit-llvm
[
.BR -O0 | -O1 | -O2 | -O3
]
[
.B -o
.I output
]

.B ocelotlc
.I source-file
.BR --emit-asm | --emit-obj
[
.BR -O0 | -O1 | -O2 | -O3
]
[
.B -o
.I output
]
[
.BI --target= triple
]
[
.BI --cpu= cpu
]
[
.BI --features= feature-string
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocelotlc
is the command-line compiler for the Ocelotl Tensor Compiler project.

Ocelotl is an experimental compiler implemented in modern C++.
Its compilation pipeline includes lexical analysis, parsing,
semantic analysis, an SSA-inspired intermediate representation,
and LLVM IR generation.

The compiler currently supports inspection of lexical tokens and
generation of LLVM intermediate representation, target assembly, and
relocatable object files for supported programs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --emit-tokens
Tokenize the input source file and print the resulting token stream.
.TP
.B --emit-llvm
Compile the input through the Ocelotl frontend, semantic analyzer,
Ocelotl intermediate representation, and LLVM backend, then print
the LLVM IR after the selected optimization pipeline.
.TP
.B --emit-llvm-before-opt
Emit verified LLVM IR immediately after lowering and before optimization.
.TP
.BR -O0 , " " -O1 , " " -O2 , " " -O3
Select LLVM's standard optimization pipeline. The default is
.BR -O0 .
.TP
.B --emit-asm
Compile the input and emit target assembly.
.TP
.B --emit-obj
Compile the input and emit a relocatable object file.
.TP
.BI -o " path"
Write output to the specified path. LLVM IR and tokens default to standard
output. Assembly and object files default to the source basename with a
.B .s
or
.B .o
suffix.
.TP
.BI --target= triple
Select and normalize the LLVM target triple. The default is the host target.
.TP
.BI --cpu= cpu
Select the target CPU.
.TP
.BI --features= feature-string
Select the comma-separated LLVM target feature string.
.PP
Target object generation does not provide a cross linker, sysroot, target C
runtime, dynamic loader, or emulator. Those are separate optional components
needed only to link or execute the generated target object.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display the tokens generated from an Ocelotl source file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ocelotlc program.oc --emit-tokens
.RE
.fi

Generate LLVM IR:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ocelotlc program.oc --emit-llvm-before-opt -O2 -o before.ll
ocelotlc program.oc --emit-llvm -O2 -o after.ll
.RE
.fi

Generate target assembly and a relocatable object:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ocelotlc program.oc --emit-asm -O2 -o program.s
ocelotlc program.oc --emit-obj -O2 -o program.o
.RE
.fi

Generate and inspect an AArch64 relocatable object:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ocelotlc program.oc --target=aarch64-linux-gnu --cpu=generic \
    --emit-obj -O2 -o program-aarch64.o
llvm-readelf -h program-aarch64.o
.RE
.fi
